                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "check to see `PCIeSlots` property exists in the Chassis first.\nThen follow the PCIeSlots['@odata.id'] link instead of hardcoding  {chassis}`/PCIeSlots`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Many Chassis resources will not have the optional `Slots` property, please guard:\n```if (Array.isArray(data.Slots) && data.Slots.length > 0)```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Hide the section if there are no slots\n```v-if=\"pcieSlots.length\"```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "If slots aren't present then we will display the `emptyMessage` i.e.,\"No items available\" in the table ,so do we really need this change to hide the section completely?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "The display should be data-driven.  If no related resources are found in the API, we should not show it.  (we need to special-case dynamic Resources of course!).  But the number of PCIe slots is physical.\nOne of our BMC platforms is a NIC, not a server.  It does not make sense to show a bunch of empty tables for resources that are not available to that platform.  In this specific case for PCIe slots, if it is not in the data it makes sense to hide the table.  For other things like memory, we make sure to show \"slots\" not populated DIMMs, but same there, if my card does not have DIMM slots, then makes no sense to show the empty DIMM table to the user."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "We can make this change, But the rest of the tables in the Inventory and LEDs page have empty message displayed.\n\nSo, Maybe we get this change in to be consistent with the rest of the page. In a future PR, maybe we can add this for all the tables?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I totally agree that we should not make this change here right now for consistency.\n\nI wanted to call out the issue however so that we can have this discussion.\n\nFYI: We are already hiding these tables downstream, the catch was dynamically showing the quick links at the top of the Inventory page."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Why hide OEM slots?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "For our internal machines we have dummy logical slots listed in slot type OEM, so thats why we are filtering out OEM slot types"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "If you wish to hide it for a specific platform, then handle that change downstream?  Even in that case I would filter it to hidden in the table by default, but still let the user see it if they would like since it is in the API (Redfish-first!)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "+1. Can we remove this check?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Inventory/InventoryTablePcieSlots.vue",
                    "line": 121,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
