                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is just getting itself, you can safely remove this line."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "This change is required as singleChassis has only: \u2028\n{\n  \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Chassis/chassis\"\n}\n\n\nAfter we make this API call (Line 39), we would get the data:\nHere, we are checking if PCIeSlots are present and then making the API call to PCIeSlots."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "I see, resolving."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "btw, downstream I have been removing some of the duplicate fetch code, I let the chassis store worry about fetching the Chassis resources and call it from the other stores that need it, something like\n```\ndispatch('chassis/getChassisInfo')\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "My previous comment on this has not been resolved.\nMy quick take was:\n```let uri = singleChassis?.PCIeSlots?.['@odata.id'];\n            if (uri) {\n              return await api\n                .get(uri)```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Same as the comment on #38, \nsingleChassis has only: \u2028\n{\n  \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Chassis/chassis\"\n}"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "The issue here is that the code is hardcoding \"/PCIeSlots\" to the end of the URI.  We should not be making these assumptions, especially since the Chassis data provides the URI:\n```\n  \"PCIeSlots\": {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Chassis/chassis/PCIeSlots\"\n  },\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Right!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "and since PCIeSlots is an optional param, it should be checked to see if it exisits first."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/HardwareStatus/PcieSlotsStore.js",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
